(footprint "AC7200_corrected"
	(version 20260206)
	(generator "pcbnew")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "ALINX AC7200 XC7A200T-2FBG484I FPGA SOM footprint for the CARRIER board (mates CON1-4 with Panasonic AXK680337YG headers). CORRECTED 2026-10-11: AC7200.kicad_mod's connector pads, mounting holes and silkscreen were mirrored in Y (STEP Y-up values copied into KiCad's Y-down frame without negation), putting CON2 on the bottom edge and reversing every connector's pin order. This footprint is AC7200.kicad_mod with every Y coordinate (and pad/text angle) negated; the 3D model offsets were already correct and are unchanged. Checked against ALINX's top-view drawing (docs/AC7200 structure PDF), ALINX's bottom-layer component drawing (docs/AC7200 PCB PDF p.2: CON labels + pin-1 dots), and the CON-labelled cad/AC7200.3.0.stp: in top view CON2 is on the JTAG-header edge (KiCad -Y). Pin names/numbers unchanged (see AC7200.kicad_sym). Still unverified, as before: exact pad size and row pitch vs Panasonic's land pattern, and the 2.7mm hole diameter. See cad/assembly/README.md.")
	(tags "ALINX AC7200 XC7A200T FPGA SOM Artix-7")
